---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Architecture from "../components/Architecture.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="GrooveNet — Vinyl collection management for DJs" description="A self-hosted, open-source system for managing, analyzing, searching, and connecting a vinyl collection." currentPath="/">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">PUBLIC VINYL RADIO / OPEN SYSTEM 001</p><h1>Make your record collection <em>legible.</em></h1><p class="lede">GrooveNet is a self-hosted system for DJs and collectors: import your Discogs collection, enrich it, analyze the audio, and use what you learn to search, discover, and sequence music.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/Public-Vinyl-Radio/groovenet" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View on GitHub ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/docs">Read the docs →</a></div></div>
    <div class="record" aria-hidden="true"><div class="record-label"><span>GN</span><small>YOUR COLLECTION<br />IN CONTEXT</small></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">NOT A STREAMING SERVICE</p><p>GrooveNet starts with the collection you’ve built in the real world. It gives that collection a useful technical memory—release data, listening metadata, audio characteristics, and links between tracks—while the records remain the point.</p></section>
  <section class="features wrap" aria-labelledby="features-title"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">CAPABILITIES / 02</p><h2 id="features-title">A working catalog, not a dashboard.</h2></div><div class="feature-list"><article><b>01 / Collection</b><h3>Import and organize</h3><p>Sync a Discogs collection, browse releases and tracks, edit in bulk, and keep the information around a physical library available when you need it.</p></article><article><b>02 / Analysis</b><h3>Listen beyond the label</h3><p>Essentia-powered audio analysis brings BPM, key, and mood into the catalog. Optional embeddings support vector similarity search.</p></article><article><b>03 / Discovery</b><h3>Find the connective tissue</h3><p>Search with full-text, fuzzy, and advanced filters; enrich tracks from Apple Music, YouTube, and SoundCloud; discover relationships across the collection.</p></article><article><b>04 / Sequencing</b><h3>Build a more coherent set</h3><p>Generate optimized playlists with a genetic algorithm using BPM, key, mood, and genre—then take your own judgment back to the decks.</p></article><article><b>05 / Interfaces</b><h3>Use it where you work</h3><p>Manage the library through the web app, a scriptable terminal client, or an MCP server that lets Claude work with your collection in natural language.</p></article><article><b>06 / Network</b><h3>Share collections</h3><p>Browse and share collections with friends, so the system can reflect the social routes through which records move and music gets passed along.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="product wrap" aria-labelledby="product-title"><div class="product-copy"><p class="eyebrow">IN USE / 03</p><h2 id="product-title">One collection. More ways in.</h2><p>The existing GrooveNet web interface is the operational view: catalog, track details, playlists, audio metadata, and the work of keeping a library useful.</p><p class="caption">Actual GrooveNet interface recording from the project repository.</p></div><figure><img src="/images/groovenet-demo.gif" width="871" height="1028" alt="Animated GrooveNet web interface showing a collection and track management views." loading="lazy" /></figure></section>
  <div class="wrap"><Architecture /></div>
  <section class="open-source"><div class="wrap open-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE / 04</p><h2>Built to be run with your records.</h2></div><div><p>GrooveNet is MIT-licensed and self-hosted. Its stack brings together a Next.js application, PostgreSQL with pgvector, Redis, Python services for audio analysis and playlist generation, and a download worker.</p><p>It is maintained by <a href="https://publicvinylradio.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Public Vinyl Radio ↗</a>—an ecosystem rooted in the practice of collecting, listening, and DJing.</p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/Public-Vinyl-Radio/groovenet" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the source ↗</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .hero { min-height: min(47rem, calc(100vh - 4.5rem)); padding: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem) 0 4rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .9fr; align-items: center; gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 8rem); overflow: hidden; } h1 { font-size: clamp(3.7rem, 8.1vw, 7.5rem); max-width: 45rem; margin-bottom: 1.7rem; } h1 em { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; } .lede { max-width: 37rem; font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.3rem); color: var(--muted); } .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; margin-top: 2rem; } .record { width: min(74vw, 30rem); justify-self: end; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; background: repeating-radial-gradient(circle, #0a0a09 0 2px, #242420 3px 5px, #11110f 6px 8px); display: grid; place-items: center; box-shadow: 0 1.3rem 2.2rem #00000066; position: relative; } .record::before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 12%; border: 1px solid #777268; border-radius: inherit; opacity: .5; } .record-label { width: 35%; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); color: var(--paper); display: grid; align-content: center; text-align: center; z-index: 1; } .record-label span { font: 800 1.1rem var(--mono); letter-spacing: -.1em; } .record-label small { margin-top: .45rem; font: .38rem/1.3 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .04em; } .intro { border-block: 1px solid var(--line); padding: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6.5rem) 0; } .intro > p:last-child { font: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 3.8rem)/1.13 var(--display); letter-spacing: -.025em; max-width: 58rem; margin: 0; } .features { padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem) 0; } .feature-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 3.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); } .feature-list article { padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 2rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); } .feature-list article:nth-child(3n+2) { padding-left: 1.25rem; border-inline: 1px solid var(--line); } .feature-list article:nth-child(3n) { padding-left: 1.25rem; } .feature-list b { font: .66rem var(--mono); color: var(--muted); } h3 { font: 500 1.7rem var(--display); letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 2.3rem 0 .5rem; } .feature-list p { font-family: var(--text); color: var(--muted); font-size: .91rem; margin: 0; max-width: 20rem; } .product { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem) 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: .75fr 1.25fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem); align-items: center; } .product-copy > p:not(.eyebrow) { font-family: var(--text); color: var(--muted); max-width: 28rem; } .caption { font: .68rem var(--mono) !important; margin-top: 3rem !important; } figure { margin: 0; background: #181816; padding: clamp(.65rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem); border: 1px solid var(--line); } figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: min(34rem, 60vw); object-fit: cover; object-position: top; } .open-source { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 5%, var(--paper)); color: var(--ink); padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem) 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--line); } .open-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4rem; } .open-source h2 { max-width: 28rem; } .open-source p { font-family: var(--text); max-width: 34rem; color: var(--muted); } .open-source a:not(.button) { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .18em; } .open-source .button { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 25%, transparent); color: var(--ink); margin-top: 1rem; } .open-source .button:hover { background: transparent; color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); } @media (max-width: 760px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: 0; } .record { justify-self: center; order: -1; width: min(68vw, 21rem); } .feature-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .feature-list article, .feature-list article:nth-child(3n+2), .feature-list article:nth-child(3n) { padding: 1.25rem 0 2rem; border-inline: 0; } .product, .open-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } figure img { height: 26rem; } }
</style>
